AB  - At the time of Industry 4.0, one ever-growing demand from warehouses is to be efficient, accurate and adaptable. This paper presents a 3-tier Conceptual Framework combining GenAI and AR for improving the efficiency in warehouses. The model serves five modules, data acquisition module, GenAI engine module, reinforcement learning module, AR-based operator interface module and a feedback loop for continuous improvement. Contrary to conventional static workflows, the methodology enables adaptive decision making, immersive operator support and real-time human–machine interaction.To offer initial validation, we performed a mini-simulation on artificial warehouse data comparing a baseline situation (manual routing and no AR) with the proposed scenario (GenAI-optimal routing and AR-enhanced picking). The simulation demonstrates reasonable performance enhancements, i.e., a 20–35% decrease in picking time; 98% inventory accuracy. These results are illustrative, not empirical, and are in line with previous AR and AI research.Certainly, the technological innovation and theoretical insights are important contributions of this work. Technologically, it showcases technology integration and modularization of GenAI & AR for smart warehouses. In the scientific context, it situates the framework in supply chain management and organization transformation studies. As a nascent Conceptual Framework that also has preliminary empirical support we provide the building blocks for future prototypes, experimental studies and theories to become integrated into smart supply chain management.
ER  - 

