AB  - English is the main language for international communication. In the Mexican context, information provided by the national education authority points out that even though English language teaching is mandatory since 2017, there is not encouraging progress on the preparation of educational institutions to fulfill the requirement, leading to identify the need of developing new strategies and tools to support the process. This paper is dedicated to describing the process that was followed for the development of ARTUI, an Augmented Reality-based application to support the English language teaching process, following a Model-driven approach. The present proposal relies on the use of Tangible User Interfaces, and the content displayed on it is based on material provided by certification entities. A description of the developed tool and its evaluation in terms of usability are provided.
