AB  - History: Background Extended Reality (XR) films are a new paradigm in immersive storytelling that combines Virtual Reality, Augmented Reality and Mixed Reality technologies, but experiences widespread issues in production inefficiency and poor audience targeting. The existing production processes involve a lot of manual efforts and do not utilize computational intelligence to optimize them. Approaches: This work suggests a smart system that will utilize Generative Adversarial Networks, Reinforcement Learning and Deep Neural networks as a three-layer model that consists of content generation, optimization of production, and matching with users. The framework fully integrates script parsing based on LSTM, automated optimization of 3D asset generation, resource scheduling using genetic algorithm and multi-modal collaborative filtering to optimize the entire workflow. Findings: Experimental validation using 500 samples of 500 XR film proves the ability to reduce the production time by 67 percent, increase the quality measures of content by 43 percent and predict user preference by 82 percent, which is much better than the conventional methods. The practical applications of the system are confirmed in the real-time personalized recommendations, latency of 45ms and user satisfaction rate of 89%. Final Thoughts: The suggested algorithmic intervention is effective in increasing the efficiency of creativity and increasing the possibility of reaching the audience of the XR film ecosystem without sacrificing the quality requirements.
