AB  - 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) enables real-time radiance field rendering, yet it still suffers from geometric degradation under sparse-view conditions and lacks the semantic grounding that interactive VR systems require. EchoSpace is a web-based VR platform that unifies semantic-aware reconstruction, automatic 3D annotation, and intelligent agent interaction into a cohesive framework. First, SA-3DGS introduces a semantic-guided optimization strategy that leverages SAM 3 masks for region-specific densification and foreground-weighted loss computation, achieving 21.13 dB PSNR on the LLFF 3-view benchmark (+0.37 dB over DropGaussian). Second, a SAM 3driven 3D annotation pipeline transforms concept-driven 2D segmentations into 3D object annotations via multi-view ray triangulation and automatic collider generation. Third, an MCP-based intelligent agent exposes 30 standardized tools for scene inspection, navigation, and manipulation, underpinned by a semantic scene graph encoding 11 spatial relationship types. Fourth, the complete system is deployed on PlayCanvas with WebGPU rendering and SOG compression (∼20×), supporting third-person character control, A* navigation, and auto-cruise. Quantitative experiments on three benchmarks and qualitative system demonstrations validate the effectiveness of the proposed framework.
ER  - 

