AB  - Eye gaze estimation rapidly becomes the required technology in virtual reality environments. The geometrical model base method is commonly used by equipping infrared (IR) light sources and cameras inside of the head mount displays (HMDs). Some HMDs enable users to wear with spectacles on, and, in this case, IR light reflections of the eyeglass often causes serious obstruction to detect those of the corneal. In a previous study, we had proposed the multi-channel CycleGAN to generate the eye images with no eyeglass from those with eyeglass. It seemed to be successful but not perfect especially in serious eyeglass reflection cases. In this study, we additionally applied the difference image equivalency loss and late fusion of channels to improve removal performance of eyeglass reflections and reduce mixing actions across channels, which achieved enhanced removal of the eyeglass reflections.
ER  - 

