AB  - The Arborist is a mixed reality (MR) installation transforms physiological signals into digital blooms, inviting participants to co-create a shared virtual ecosystem through embodied interaction. Rather than storing raw bio-signals, the system maps heart rate, skin conductance, and temperature to generative visual and sonic parameters, rendering internal states as ambient, non-indexical forms. Users grow and place digital flowers on a tree, transitioning between MR and virtual reality (VR) through gesture. The evolving visual archive preserves only aesthetic traces of presence. Rooted in posthuman and participatory design, the work reimagines biometric data as poetic, collaborative memory connecting past and future.
ER  - 

