AB  - This paper examines the development of an adaptable virtual reality non-player character (VR NPC) that employs AI-enabled conversation through text and audio for immersive interaction with VR users with mental health problems. The project aims to lessen the impact of people undergoing psychological trauma through AI integration by enabling a real-time calming NPC interaction. This application is useful for people with mental illness like anxiety, depression, Autism Spectrum Disorder (ASD), or post traumatic stress disorder (PTSD) as it offers companionship during difficult situations. The possible settings include, but are not limited to, personal therapeutic, mental health counseling, recreational, sleep-inducing, and even medical ones. In most cases, the VR companion can be employed in hospitals or other medical institutions to reduce patients' pre-and post-operative anxiety to lower pain and tension, thus improving overall patient experience. This project seeks to create an emotionally responsive environment to aid individuals with evident mental health challenges, employing the power of virtual reality and artificial intelligence technologies for free form conversation on platforms like Meta Quest 3 via Unity, with special emphasis on emotional well-being.
ER  - 

